"],["Kyoto Municipal Museum of Art","sight",35.01284,135.78357,"Okazaki Park, Sakyō-ku","Tue-Sun 09:00-17:00","","","","r","This museum houses a wide variety of art with the permanent collections featuring artists that are from Kyoto. Special exhibits may feature Japanese art from other areas or foreign artwork."],["Kyoto National Museum of Modern Art","sight",35.01239,135.78194,"Okazaki Enshōji-chō, Sakyō-ku","Tue-Sun 09:30-17:00 (on Fridays during special exhibitions, hours may be extended to 20:00)","","","","r","An interesting museum featuring works from famous, as well as up-and-coming modern artists. Exhibits change frequently, so it's best to call or visit the website to see exactly what will featured during your visit. You may also want to…"],["Kyoto City Zoo","sight",35.01285,135.78601,"Okazaki Hōshōji-cho, Sakyō-ku","","","","","r","Like most zoos, visitors will see lions, tigers, and monkeys. There is an aviary and reptile exhibit, as well. The zoo has some native Japanese animals, but there isn't much to set it apart from most other zoos in the world."],["Okazaki Shrine","sight",35.01742,135.78878,"","","","","","r","A Shinto shrine traditionally believed to have been established in 794, when Emperor Kanmu moved the capital to Heian-kyō. It was one of four shrines built to protect the new capital, and was known as Higashi-Tenno (Eastern Heavenly…"],["Kōdai-ji Temple","sight",35.00076,135.78111,"526, Shimogawara-chō, Kōdai-ji, Higashiyama-ku","Daily 09:00-17:00","","","","r","This temple was built for Toyotomi Hideyoshi's widow by Tokugawa Ieyasu and is located right next to the Ryōzen Kannon temple on the Higashiyama mountain. If you really like temples this is a very nice one. It's got a nice bamboo grove…"],["Chion-in","sight",35.00617,135.78328,"","","","","","r","The head temple of the Jodo sect of Buddhism. The Sanmon gate at the entrance to the temple is the largest of such gates in the nation. Visitors can walk freely around the complex and inside the buildings, except for those that house…"],["Shōren-in","sight",35.00731,135.7832,"69-1 Sanjōbō-chō","Daily 09:00-17:00","","","","r","Once associated with the head Tendai Buddhist sect temple, Enryaku-ji on Mount Hiei, Shōren-in is considered to be one of the top five Tendai sect temples. During the Tokugawa period, it served as temporary lodging for a retired emperor…"],["Higashi Ōtani Mausoleum","sight",35.00147,135.78249,"","","","","","r","Located in a cemetery, tourists typically visit this site accidentally however, because some of the ashes of Shinran, the founder of Jōdo-Shin Buddhism, are contained inside the mausoleum, it is a popular place for Buddhists to come to…"],["Kōun-ji","sight",35.01701,135.79519,"","","","","","r","A temple designed around the borrowed scenery of the surrounding mountains, it was once owned by Empress Go-mizunoo."],["Nyakuoji Shrine","sight",35.01574,135.79631,"2 Nishioji Sakyo-ku","","","","","r","Established in 1160, a nice shrine to visit in the autumn when the leaves are changing. It's a worthwhile stop for those travelling along the Philosopher's Path, but probably not worth making the trip just to see this shrine."],["Eikandō Temple","sight",35.01437,135.79557,"48 Eikandō-chō, Sakyō-ku","Daily 09:00&ndash;17:00","","","","r","A large temple said to have been constructed by Priest Kūkai. The temple features a unique statue of Amida Buddha, Mikaeri Amida, that looks to the right rather than facing forward; there's a charming legend attached to it. The temple…"],["Nanzenji Temple","sight",35.01127,135.79308,"Fukuchi-cho, Nanzenji, Sakyo-ku","08:40-17:00 (until 16:30 from Dec to Feb)","","","","r","with its distinctive two-story entrance gate (sanmon) and aqueduct, is another popular temple in Kyoto, but its larger size means that it doesn't seem as crowded as many of the others. Nearest bus stop: Nanzenji, Eikando-michi. Nearest…"],["Toryanse","restaurant",35.01537,135.79494,"","","","","","r","A restaurant with vegan options. The interior features photos of cat that roam around the Philosopher’s Path. Cash only."],["Kikunoi (main restaurant)","restaurant",35.0018,135.78199,"459 Shimokawara-cho, Yasakatoriimae-sagaru, Shimokawara-dori","11:30-13:00, 17:00-20:00","","","","r","One of Japan's most famous ryotei, serving kaiseki using the finest regional seasonal ingredients. Very expensive for dinner, but lunches are much more reasonable. Bookings essential well in advance. Staff don't speak much English, but…"]]}